[[Burawa]] is a country located in [[Kaftia]]. Burawa is a {{w|Socialist}} {{w|semi-presidential republic}} of 128 million people bordering [[Borders of Burawa|9 countries by land]], it is the largest country in Kaftia by population and second largest by area behind [[Enfolo]]. The country is divided into [[Administrative divisions of Burawa|86 independent urban administrations, 34 rural administrations, and 8 metropolitan administrations]] with it's capital being [[Kankadadka]]. 

Burawa's name comes from it's progenitor state of the [[Empire of Burawa]] that occupied most of southern Kaftia until the end of the 18th century. The lands where Burawa exists today were settled by early humans as early as 25,000 years ago during the initial migrations from central Kaftia. The earliest state to form in the region was the [[Ancient Ufyen|Ufyen]] near modern day [[Badalga]]. The land during the Iron age had become home to small kingdoms along it's coast that traded along the [[Mesogean Sea]]. The first [[Kingdom of Burawa|Burawi kingdom]] had formed as an [[Badan alliances|marriage alliance]] of city-states in [[Unification of Mazar and Iskhal|403]] between the [[Mazar (City State)|Mazar]] and [[Kingdom of Iskhal|Iskhal]] to increase influence along the Dafar river to Badalga. The kingdom by the 16th century due to conquests of it's northern and eastern territories had become a vast feudal empire, stretching from modern day [[Shedou]] to [[Ayorin]]. By the end of the century Burawa was plunged into the [[Long decades war|long decades war]] that split influence of the subcontinent between the [[Western Burawi Empire]] and the [[Empire of Burawa|Eastern Burawi Empire]], where current day Burawa stems from. The two empires, split down the [[Dimar River]], [[Faheya Sea]] and [[Kitale River]] continued to survive until the 18th and 19th centuries.

The last emperor the Eastern Burawi emperor, [[Cawil III]] had abdicated in 1832, as part of the [[Samara Deceleration]], forming the first Burawi Republic. The nation had quickly industrialized and became a major economic power in the world. The nation had experienced rapid population growth during the end of the 19th century and an massive increase in economic inequality that lead to the rise of socialist groups gaining electoral power in the government. By 1930 the socialist parties had controlled a super-majority of seats in parliment, mainly [[Maana Kadar]]'s [[Socialist Party of Burawa|Socialist Party]] and had legislated a new constitution of the country, [[Partition of Burawa|dividing the state]] into 7 new countries. The central state of Burawa had emerged in 1932, banning non-socialist aligned parties and nationalized many industries, ensuing political conflict lead to the [[Burawa Domestic War]], which had factions of non-socialist groups aligned with foreign interests attempt to restore the previous government, the war had been cut short due to the [[Great Adonian War]] that had seen Burawa invaded by it's sourthern neighbor of [[Volisania]].

Burawa is a highly developed country and is the 5th largest economy by purchasing power parity. It is one of the world's largest exporters and major influence in the [[Adonian community]]. The country remains very influential in it's former colonies and is a major tourist destination due to its relative low cost of living.

== Etymology ==
Burawa comes from the [[Ufyen Language|Ufyen]] word for the land of the mighty river, specifically [[Buran River]] that travels between [[Lake Haro]] and the [[Mesogean Sea]].